    Note over Alice,Network: ═══════════ KEY ARCHITECTURE FEATURES ═══════════

    rect rgb(240, 240, 255)
        Note over Alice,Network: 🏗️ COLLECTIVE TREE ARCHITECTURE:<br/><br/>1. TREE MERGING (Individual → Collective):<br/>   📝 Input: Multiple individual trees<br/>   🔄 Process: Hash-based node merging<br/>   📊 Output: Unified collective tree<br/>   💡 Each node tracks contributor data<br/><br/>2. NODE RECOGNITION METRICS:<br/>   - Total Recognition: Weighted sum of contributor points<br/>   - Average MRD: Consensus measure (how many agree)<br/>   - Contributor Weights: Per-contributor influence<br/>   - Path Analysis: Tree structure metadata<br/><br/>3. GOVERNANCE FILTERING:<br/>   🎯 Recognition-based: min_total_recognition, min_average_mrd<br/>   👥 Consensus-based: min_contributor_count, min_percentage<br/>   🔧 Logic-based: JSON Logic rules (complex criteria)<br/>   🛠️ Custom: User-defined filter functions<br/>   📏 Path preservation: Keep parent paths when child filtered<br/><br/>4. DISTRIBUTION MODES:<br/>   🎯 Single-Node: Focus on one specific node<br/>   🌲 Tree-Wide: Aggregate across entire tree<br/>   ⚖️ Weighted-Path: Weight by tree position<br/>   🔢 Normalization: sum-to-one or proportional<br/><br/>5. CAPACITY ALLOCATION:<br/>   📋 Capacity Slots: Available resources to allocate<br/>   💼 Member Commitments: Who provides what<br/>   ✅ Compliance Filtering: Match providers to recipients<br/>   ⚖️ Share-Based Distribution: Allocate by recognition shares<br/>   🔄 Reallocation: Handle declined capacity<br/><br/>6. SEPARATION OF CONCERNS:<br/>   Individual Trees = User inputs (stable)<br/>   Collective Tree = Merged perspective (derived)<br/>   Node Recognition = Metrics (derived)<br/>   Distribution = Shares (derived)<br/>   Allocation = Resources (derived)<br/>   <br/>   Only individual trees stored permanently<br/>   Everything else recomputed on demand
    end

    Note over Alice,Network: ═══════════ ADVANCED FEATURE 1: HASH-BASED NODE IDENTITY ═══════════

    rect rgb(255, 245, 245)
        Note over Collective: 🔑 NODE HASHING FOR MERGING
        Collective->>Collective: Hash-based node identification:<br/><br/>Node Identity = hash(node_name + node_type + path)<br/><br/>Example:<br/>  Alice's tree: "Food Security" Goal at path ["root"]<br/>  Carol's tree: "Food Security" Goal at path ["root"]<br/>  Bob's tree: "Community Health" Goal at path ["root"]<br/><br/>Hash calculation:<br/>  hash("Food Security" + "Goal" + "root")<br/>    = "fs_goal_root_abc123"<br/>  <br/>  hash("Community Health" + "Goal" + "root")<br/>    = "ch_goal_root_def456"<br/><br/>Merging logic:<br/>  If same hash → merge properties<br/>  If different hash → separate nodes<br/><br/>Result:<br/>  "Food Security" from Alice + Carol → 1 merged node<br/>  "Community Health" from Bob → separate node<br/><br/>Benefits:<br/>  ✓ Automatic node matching across contributors<br/>  ✓ No manual ID coordination needed<br/>  ✓ Semantic merging (same meaning = same node)<br/>  ✓ Works with any number of contributors
    end

    Note over Alice,Network: ═══════════ ADVANCED FEATURE 2: MRD (MULTI-RECOGNITION DEPTH) ═══════════

    rect rgb(245, 255, 245)
        Note over Collective: 📊 CONSENSUS MEASUREMENT
        Collective->>Collective: Multi-Recognition Depth (MRD):<br/><br/>Definition:<br/>  MRD = (# contributors who recognize node) / (total contributors)<br/><br/>Example 1: High Consensus<br/>  Node: "Food Security"<br/>  Contributors: 3 total [Alice, Bob, Carol]<br/>  Recognizers: 3 [Alice, Bob, Carol all have this node]<br/>  MRD = 3/3 = 1.0 (100% consensus!) ✓<br/><br/>Example 2: Partial Consensus<br/>  Node: "Community Health"<br/>  Contributors: 3 total<br/>  Recognizers: 2 [Bob, Carol have it, Alice doesn't]<br/>  MRD = 2/3 = 0.667 (67% consensus)<br/><br/>Example 3: Low Consensus<br/>  Node: "Bob's Pet Project"<br/>  Contributors: 3 total<br/>  Recognizers: 1 [only Bob]<br/>  MRD = 1/3 = 0.333 (33% consensus) ⚠️<br/><br/>Governance Use:<br/>  min_average_mrd: 0.5 → Require >50% consensus<br/>  Filters out nodes with low collective support<br/><br/>Benefits:<br/>  ✓ Measures agreement, not just recognition weight<br/>  ✓ Prevents single contributor from dominating<br/>  ✓ Encourages collective alignment<br/>  ✓ Simple, intuitive metric (0.0 to 1.0)
    end

    Note over Alice,Network: ═══════════ ADVANCED FEATURE 3: JSON LOGIC FILTERING ═══════════

    rect rgb(245, 245, 255)
        Note over Collective: 🔧 COMPLEX GOVERNANCE RULES
        Collective->>Collective: JSON Logic integration for flexible rules:<br/><br/>Example 1: Simple threshold<br/>  {<br/>    ">=": [{"var": "total_recognition"}, 50]<br/>  }<br/>  → Keep nodes with total_recognition >= 50<br/><br/>Example 2: AND condition<br/>  {<br/>    "and": [<br/>      {">=": [{"var": "average_mrd"}, 0.7]},<br/>      {">=": [{"var": "contributor_count"}, 3]}<br/>    ]<br/>  }<br/>  → Keep if MRD >= 0.7 AND count >= 3<br/><br/>Example 3: OR with complex logic<br/>  {<br/>    "or": [<br/>      {">=": [{"var": "total_recognition"}, 100]},<br/>      {"and": [<br/>        {">=": [{"var": "average_mrd"}, 0.9]},<br/>        {">=": [{"var": "contributor_count"}, 5]}<br/>      ]}<br/>    ]<br/>  }<br/>  → Keep if (recognition >= 100) OR<br/>           (MRD >= 0.9 AND count >= 5)<br/><br/>Example 4: Nested conditions<br/>  {<br/>    "if": [<br/>      {"==": [{"var": "depth"}, 0]},<br/>      true,  // Always keep root<br/>      {">=": [{"var": "average_mrd"}, 0.5]}<br/>    ]<br/>  }<br/>  → Root always kept, others need MRD >= 0.5<br/><br/>Benefits:<br/>  ✓ Declarative (not imperative code)<br/>  ✓ Serializable (store in DB/network)<br/>  ✓ Platform-agnostic (works in any language)<br/>  ✓ Composable (combine multiple rules)<br/>  ✓ Safe (no arbitrary code execution)
    end

    Note over Alice,Network: ═══════════ ADVANCED FEATURE 4: CONTRIBUTOR WEIGHT CALCULATION ═══════════

    rect rgb(255, 250, 240)
        Note over Collective: ⚖️ WEIGHTED MERGING
        Collective->>Collective: calculateContributorWeights({<br/>  contributorIds: ["Alice", "Bob", "Carol"],<br/>  contributorTrees: Map {<br/>    Alice → aliceTree,<br/>    Bob → bobTree,<br/>    Carol → carolTree<br/>  },<br/>  recognitionShares: {<br/>    Alice: 0.5,  // Optional: explicit weights<br/>    Bob: 0.3,<br/>    Carol: 0.2<br/>  }<br/>})<br/><br/>MODE 1: Explicit Recognition Shares<br/>  If recognitionShares provided:<br/>    Use as-is (already normalized)<br/>    Alice: 0.5, Bob: 0.3, Carol: 0.2 ✓<br/><br/>MODE 2: Equal Weights (Default)<br/>  If no recognitionShares:<br/>    weights = 1.0 / count<br/>    Alice: 0.333, Bob: 0.333, Carol: 0.333<br/><br/>MODE 3: Mutual Fulfillment (Future)<br/>  Calculate from network relationships:<br/>    MF(Alice,Bob) = 0.8<br/>    MF(Alice,Carol) = 0.6<br/>    MF(Bob,Carol) = 0.7<br/>    <br/>    Weight_Alice = Σ(MF with others) / total<br/>    Weight_Bob = Σ(MF with others) / total<br/>    Weight_Carol = Σ(MF with others) / total<br/><br/>Properties propagation:<br/>  When merging node properties (points, weights, etc.):<br/>    merged_value = Σ(contributor_weight × contributor_value)<br/>  <br/>  Example:<br/>    Alice says node has 70 points (weight: 0.5)<br/>    Bob says node has 50 points (weight: 0.3)<br/>    Carol says node has 80 points (weight: 0.2)<br/>    <br/>    merged_points = 0.5×70 + 0.3×50 + 0.2×80<br/>                  = 35 + 15 + 16 = 66 points
    end

    Note over Alice,Network: ═══════════ ADVANCED FEATURE 5: PATH PRESERVATION IN FILTERING ═══════════

    rect rgb(250, 245, 255)
        Note over Collective: 🌲 MAINTAINING TREE STRUCTURE
        Collective->>Collective: Path Preservation During Filtering:<br/><br/>Scenario:<br/>  Tree structure:<br/>    Root<br/>      → Goal A (recognition: 100) ✓<br/>          → Goal A1 (recognition: 20) ❌<br/>              → Goal A1a (recognition: 80) ✓<br/>          → Goal A2 (recognition: 90) ✓<br/>      → Goal B (recognition: 30) ❌<br/>          → Goal B1 (recognition: 70) ✓<br/><br/>Filter: min_total_recognition = 50<br/><br/>preserve_paths: false<br/>  Apply filter strictly:<br/>    Root ✓ (always kept)<br/>      → Goal A ✓ (100 >= 50)<br/>          → Goal A2 ✓ (90 >= 50)<br/>      (Goal A1 removed, so A1a orphaned and removed)<br/>      (Goal B removed, so B1 orphaned and removed)<br/>  <br/>  Result: 3 nodes (Root, A, A2)<br/><br/>preserve_paths: true<br/>  Keep parent paths to preserved nodes:<br/>    Root ✓<br/>      → Goal A ✓ (meets filter)<br/>          → Goal A1 ✓ (kept as path to A1a!)<br/>              → Goal A1a ✓ (meets filter)<br/>          → Goal A2 ✓ (meets filter)<br/>      → Goal B ✓ (kept as path to B1!)<br/>          → Goal B1 ✓ (meets filter)<br/>  <br/>  Result: 7 nodes (all paths preserved)<br/><br/>Use Cases:<br/>  preserve_paths: false<br/>    → Strict governance (only strong nodes)<br/>    → Clean, minimal tree<br/>  <br/>  preserve_paths: true<br/>    → Inclusive governance (keep weaker parents)<br/>    → Maintain semantic structure<br/>    → Better for UI/navigation<br/><br/>Implementation:<br/>  1. Mark nodes meeting criteria<br/>  2. If preserve_paths: Mark all ancestors<br/>  3. Filter: Keep marked nodes only<br/>  4. Renormalize weights in filtered tree
    end

    Note over Alice,Network: ═══════════ ADVANCED FEATURE 6: RENORMALIZATION ═══════════

    rect rgb(255, 245, 250)
        Note over Collective: 🔢 WEIGHT ADJUSTMENT AFTER FILTERING
        Collective->>Collective: renormalizeCollectiveTree(filteredTree):<br/><br/>Problem:<br/>  After filtering, sibling weights don't sum to 1.0<br/>  <br/>  Before filter:<br/>    Parent<br/>      → Child A (weight: 0.4)<br/>      → Child B (weight: 0.3)<br/>      → Child C (weight: 0.3)<br/>    Sum: 1.0 ✓<br/>  <br/>  After filter (removed Child B):<br/>    Parent<br/>      → Child A (weight: 0.4)<br/>      → Child C (weight: 0.3)<br/>    Sum: 0.7 ❌ (not normalized!)<br/><br/>Solution: Renormalize sibling weights<br/>  <br/>  Calculate sum: 0.4 + 0.3 = 0.7<br/>  Divide each by sum:<br/>    Child A: 0.4 / 0.7 = 0.571<br/>    Child C: 0.3 / 0.7 = 0.429<br/>  Sum: 1.0 ✓<br/><br/>Algorithm:<br/>  function renormalizeNodeRecursive(node):<br/>    // First, renormalize all children recursively<br/>    for child in node.children:<br/>      renormalizeNodeRecursive(child)<br/>    <br/>    // Then renormalize this level<br/>    if node.children.length > 0:<br/>      sum = Σ(child.weight for child in children)<br/>      if sum > 0:<br/>        for child in children:<br/>          child.weight = child.weight / sum<br/>    <br/>    return node<br/><br/>Properties:<br/>  ✓ Maintains relative proportions<br/>  ✓ Ensures valid probability distribution<br/>  ✓ Required after filtering<br/>  ✓ Applied recursively (bottom-up)
    end

