        Note over Alice,Network: 🔗 HOW COLLECTIVE TREES FIT INTO V6 PROTOCOL:<br/><br/>STRUCTURE.MD (Individual Trees):<br/>  1. User publishes tree (user inputs)<br/>  2. System computes derived state (reactive)<br/>  3. Calculate ShareOfGeneralSatisfaction<br/>  4. Calculate Mutual-Satisfaction<br/>  5. Allocate capacity (two-tier)<br/>  6. Recipients rate satisfaction<br/>  7. Satisfaction flows up tree (aggregation)<br/>  8. Shares update reactively<br/>  9. Next cycle uses updated shares<br/><br/>COLLECTIVE-STRUCTURE (Collective Layer):<br/>  1. Collect individual trees from network<br/>  2. Merge trees → collective tree<br/>  3. Calculate node recognition metrics<br/>  4. Apply governance filters<br/>  5. Generate distribution shares<br/>  6. Allocate pooled capacity<br/>  7. (Satisfaction still flows in individual trees)<br/>  8. Next governance cycle uses updated trees<br/><br/>KEY RELATIONSHIPS:<br/><br/>Individual ShareOfGeneralSatisfaction →<br/>  Used as recognitionShares in merging<br/><br/>Individual tree satisfaction →<br/>  Propagates into merged node properties<br/><br/>Collective distribution →<br/>  Used for pooled resource allocation<br/>  Complements individual allocations<br/><br/>SEPARATION OF CONCERNS:<br/>  Individual Trees = Personal autonomy<br/>  Collective Trees = Group coordination<br/>  <br/>  Both coexist, serve different purposes<br/>  Collective layer builds on individual layer<br/>  Individual trees remain source of truth
